Z||000000||FieroKyle||08-16-2001||10:13 PM||||I got my information from the "official" 2002 car guide. I made my own paragraph up though so you can give me credit there.<P>Pontiac has once again created an American mid-engined wonder. The Pontiac Speedster. It has the same 4-cyclinder that the Opel Speedster uses producing a 150 hp. Originally not to be sold in America, Pontiac has now seriously considered doing so with the slain of the late great muscle car.......the Trans Am Firebird. To keep its "driving excitement" image and sporty car production, it is quite possible that the Pontiac Speedster will be sold in America. Its a two seater convertable that some what resembles a body of a Cavilier and a Chevy Metro. Your thoughts????? I don't like it. I think its a piss poor job in making a sports car to replace the Trans Am that has a Fiero-like car to it but nothing as great as the Fiero ever was. I think a better way of saying it as they are trying to use todays style of cars with the Fiero mid-engined concept. Thats just my opinion.<P>In other 2002 car news, Porsche makes an SUV that has the front end of a Boxster and the rear similar to a Subaru Outback.||||reg||9
