Z||000013||Yellow88GT||08-17-2001||08:29 AM||||I was looking at Vauxhall's web site.<BR>The list price for the VX220<BR>(Vauxhall's re-bagged Opel Speedster)<BR>is at 22,995 British pounds.<BR>That would put it over $34,000 US,<BR>at the current exchange rates. <P>Unfortunately, I think a $20,000 price tag<BR>for a Lotus based car is wishful thinking.<P>Here's to wishing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jerry<p>[This message has been edited by Yellow88GT (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||08-17-2001||10:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Hellooooooooo Pontiac. Make a perfect copy of the Ferrari Modena with a supercharged 3800, except put a trademark 'split' Pontiac grill in it. Sell as many as fast as you can before you get sued. Oh and keep price under $20,000.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll drink to that!<P>I don't think that Pontiac will sell enough Speedster clones to make it worth their trouble. Especially at $34,000.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>We're too used to our creature comforts.<P>For that kind of money, I'll buy an Acura 3.2 TL-S. (Donning Nomex) <P> <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
