Z||000017||TI_3VOM||08-17-2001||04:00 PM||||...maybe it's just me, but didn't I read in another thread that GM WAS NOT going to bring over the Speedster due to crashworthiness problems? BTW, I read that same article (months ago); yes, it would be a nice addition for GM (Saturn, perhaps?), but I doubt it could/would take the place of the Fiero. And let's not forget the current GM mindset of lowering costs by having more than one division produce a vehicle off of the same frame, Corvette excluded (as always).  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Just had an idea: anyone look at a naked Corvette frame? Compare that to a naked Fiero frame. (See where I'm going with this?) All we need to do is use off-the -shelf components (in the spirit of the original Fiero), and there we are!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   Ahh, what about the Corvette Mafia? Well, let's placate them with a promise to only use the 3800 series V-6. The GT could use the supercharged version. (of course, if we wanted to tweek them a bit, we could form a SLP-type company to produce the GTO...with Northstar power  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">... take that, Vette, NSX, Supra TT, and all comers)<BR>...of course, that's just my opinion.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000018||Fformula88||08-17-2001||04:46 PM||||Even if it appeared over here, its not going to be cheap or plentiful.  I think their current production capacity is in the ballpark of 2000 units a year.  They have plans to add on to their factory, which would double production.  Since the first half would continue to stay in Europe, that would only leave about 2000 a year to come over to the US.  Since GM didn't sell enough Fiero's to make it worth their while (or Firebirds for that matter), I don't think they would be very interested in such a low volume car.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
