Z||000020||Doni Hagan||08-17-2001||06:47 PM||||$34K, eh? <BR>For that kind of cake, I'll buy a baby Beemer ragtop. The Caddy Catera is essentially a rebodied Opel and GM can't seem to get a handle on how to really sell it. The "bird" campaign was cute, I guess, but seemed to sit right between the demographics they (GM)really wanted to reach..... Generation X'ers and Enthusiasts. Kind of like a blooper in center field. Too hard for a bunt but too soft for a home run. <P>I don't think Pontiac has the cajones to try it without "luxury-ing" the fun out of it.  <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000021||dlancer407||08-17-2001||07:48 PM||||Remember the days when you were single, worked a minimum wage job or a little better?<BR>You could save up a little cash and go to your local dealership and buy a TransAm,Fiero<BR>AMX, Mustang or just about any muscle car you wanted. I do. It was called the 70's.The auto manufactures just don't understand why more young people are not buying there sport coupes. In 1973 I was earning about $ 3.80 an hour, and my new 1973 AMC Javelin AMX with all the toys cost me $ 4,500.00.  Now minimum wage is $ 5.15 an hour and a new TransAm costs around $26,000.00. If they would just do the math they could figure it out. Well that's the end of my rant. ||||reg||6
Z||000022||maryjane||08-17-2001||08:40 PM||||Dlancer, you're right on the money! How many young kids can make enough to save 30K? By the time they could, they have families to support, so their dream is gone before it gets here. BUT, that's where the Fiero's come in. So, I guess it works out in the Fiero god's scheme of things.||||reg||1
Z||000023||FieroKyle||08-17-2001||10:53 PM||||Kids can afford the cars (older ones in good condition, 5.0s, Fieros, Trans Am, Camaros) its what kills it is insurance companies. Alright I am kid so here, I can give ya a run down..........<P>Kids don't have to worry about housing, food, clothes so much as adults. Kids really own nothing except a car till about 18 to 25. With all this money coming in to go no where except may be for hobbies, fun, ect.... Thus money can be saved for a sports car. Well the cars I mentioned above in really good condition with low miles runs 4k to 8k. This really isn't all that much plus may be a 1k winter beater. Well the insurance for full coverage is gonna be about 1600K for 9 months plus storage for winter. Then may be PLPD for the winter beater for 3 months for about $400 there for insurance. Plus if these older cars break down which they often do and you no nothing about how to fix cars, like 95% of kids these days, you pay top dollar for a couple hours of service. Then with these high gas prices, that doesn't help either. So its not really the car itself, its the stuff that goes with owning a car that hurts kids these days.<P>I have put blood sweat and tears in just keeping my Fiero on the road this summer with gas and insurance. Plus new tires, and this and that and a stereo. The stereo is really the only thing that I wanted to put on the car, everything else was needed. Luckily my parents have helped me out with a couple of loans. My tab is only $250 right now. HaHa. and there are many kids at school with cool cars that go through the same frustrations as I do. Most people look at us like were dumb, but its what we like to do, its our hobbie. Over the past year I have become really almost obbsessive with Fieros, I am sure most of you are too, lol. I eat, sleep, work for my Fiero. Its my life.||||reg||8
Z||000024||Adam Mayer||08-17-2001||10:59 PM||||the 2.2L four is actually a hotter version of the engine used in an American car already, the Saturn L200 sedan. Because of this many have speculated that the Speedster, if it comes over the seas,will be sold as a Saturn rather than a Pontiac. My understanding is that it does use the spaceframe design, so perhaps it is a better fit as a Saturn. ||||reg||1
